# Definition of Done

A feature is complete only when applicable UI, backend, schema migration, RLS,
validation, audit event, loading/empty/success/failure states, responsive behavior,
accessibility, and important tests are implemented.

Before completion:

- confirm every visible control works or is clearly unavailable;
- confirm no duplicate component/module, fake production data, secret exposure,
  hard-coded authorization, or RLS bypass was introduced;
- run relevant tests, RLS ALLOW/DENY checks, TypeScript, ESLint, and production
  build; and
- report IMPLEMENTED, FILES CHANGED, DATABASE CHANGES, SECURITY/RLS CHANGES,
  TESTS ADDED, TEST RESULTS, BUILD RESULT, and KNOWN LIMITATIONS.
